# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EMAILJS — CONTACT FORM CREDENTIALS
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (or set these in your hosting env, e.g. Vercel)
# and fill in your real values from https://dashboard.emailjs.com/admin
#   SERVICE_ID  → "Email Services" tab → the Service ID (e.g. service_abc123)
#   TEMPLATE_ID → "Email Templates" tab → the Template ID (e.g. template_xyz789)
#   PUBLIC_KEY  → "Account" → "General" → Public Key (formerly called API Key)
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   • Replace the three values below with your real credentials.
#   • Never commit .env.local (covered by .gitignore).
#   • Make sure the variable names in your EmailJS template match the params
#     sent from the contact form: from_name, reply_to, message, to_name.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=YOUR_SERVICE_ID
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=YOUR_TEMPLATE_ID
NEXT_PUBLIC_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=YOUR_PUBLIC_KEY